window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"lillia","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 1-5","text":"A pure spacing duel: your kite against his marks. Win it with footwork, never with commitment."},{"when":"Locke 6 + first item","text":"His Purgatory is a kill button your speed cannot outrun once you are low — never trade below half in this window."},{"when":"Your two-plus items","text":"Sleep scaling for teamfights matches his pick game — grouped, you are worth more than he is."},{"text":"His W burns his own health then refunds part of the damage he took, and it is back every 18s at rank 1 — land Grievous Wounds before that refund resolves or the whole trade is undone.","when":"Every 18s"}],"wants":{"you":["Win the spacing duel with passive speed","Stay high-HP through his item window","Scale sleep for the teamfight phase"],"foe":["Slow you with marks and close","Cash in the Purgatory window","Pick you off before fights start"]},"early":"A footwork lane: your Blooming Blows speed kites, his marks slow and punish, and every stage through 5 rewards the better-positioned player rather than either kit. Poke the edge of Q onto him when he steps up to CS, respect his level-3 dash, and do not gamble — there is no scripted kill here.","mid":"The one stage with an owner is his: at first item, Purgatory becomes a kill button that your escape and sustain simply cannot answer if you are caught low. Track his cooldowns, hold the W dash for his engage, and if you must trade in this window, do it at full health with the wave near your tower.","late":"Post-items it balances again — his pick threat against your teamfight sleep, and a grouped Lillia is worth more than a roaming Locke. Stay with your team, flank fights so R catches multiple targets, and let him waste minutes hunting a pick you refuse to offer him.","whys":["Level 1 is even — you kite with Blooming Blows while he slows with marks; neither has a kill.","Skill spacing decides level 2; neither side has a reliable kill threat.","Your kite against his mark punish stays even through level 3.","Levels 4-5 remain a spacing duel with no clear favourite.","Level 6 stays even — your poke trades into his grey-health, and neither ult wins it outright yet.","Purgatory at first item hands him a kill button your escape and sustain cannot answer.","Post-items it evens out — your teamfight sleep scaling matches his pick threat."]});
