window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"lillia","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Zaahen level 3","text":"His Q-E close comes online before your passive ramps — the free-poke phase of the lane is over."},{"when":"Your level 6","text":"Lullaby is the equalizer: a slept engage is a dead engage, so the lane becomes fightable again."},{"when":"His first item","text":"Durability plus sustain out-lasts your chip — stop trying to whittle him down solo."},{"when":"Side lanes late","text":"He crushes the 1v1 — take your sleep to teamfights and leave him an empty lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke before his engage exists","Hold the W dash for his close","Trade the lane for teamfight value"],"foe":["Run you down on W cooldown","Out-sustain your chip damage","Trap you in side-lane duels"]},"early":"Enjoy the first two levels — your poke is free while his gap-close is not online — because level 3 changes the contract: his Q and E reach your squishy frame before Blooming Blows ramps up. From there he walks you down whenever your Q speed stacks lapse, so never poke without them rolling.","mid":"Level 6 hands you a genuine equalizer: Lullaby flips any engage he mistimes, and a sleeping bruiser is a dead one if your jungler is near. But once his first item lands, his durability and sustain out-last your chip — stop hunting the solo kill and start playing for the map instead.","late":"Never take the two-item side-lane duel; he wins it every time. Your value lives elsewhere: clear waves from max range, flank teamfights, and sleep three people while your team follows up. Trade him an empty lane for won fights and he ends up isolated and irrelevant.","whys":["Level 1 is even farm — you poke, but you cannot hard-punish yet.","Level 2 stays a skill mirror: your passive has not ramped and his gap-closer is not online.","Level 3 tilts to him — his Q and E close on your squishy frame before Blooming Blows stacks.","Levels 4-5 favour him: he walks you down whenever your Q speed stacks drop.","Level 6 is a skill-check — your R Lullaby can flip his mistimed engage.","At first item his durability and sustain out-scale your early chip damage.","Two items in he crushes you in any one-on-one side-lane duel."]});
