window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"lillia","b":"masteryi","win":["Lillia","Lillia","Skill","Skill","Skill","Master Yi","Master Yi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Levels 1-2","text":"Pure kite: passive speed and W poke chunk a melee champion with no tools yet — take everything on offer."},{"when":"Yi level 3","text":"Alpha Strike is 20s at rank 1 and untargetable — poke only with an exit already planned."},{"when":"Your level 6","text":"Lullaby is the fight-decider: a slept Yi dies, a missed sleep means you run."},{"when":"Yi first item onward","text":"He catches and deletes you the moment the kiting slips, and Highlander ignores your slow."}],"wants":{"you":["Chunk him before Alpha exists","Land Lullaby on his engage","Stay untouchable with W and speed"],"foe":["Alpha through your poke","Bait out your sleep first","Ignore your slow under Highlander"]},"early":"Feast early: at 1-2 your passive speed and Watch Out! poke torture a melee champion with no answers, so chunk him off every CS. From 3 his Alpha Strike buys him engages and dodge-frames — keep poking, but always with W or the river exit ready, because overextending is now punishable.","mid":"Six makes every fight a question with one answer: does Lullaby land? A slept Yi under your Q-W follow-up dies; a baited sleep means you sprint for tower. Play the ult like the entire matchup lives inside it — because once his first attack-speed item arrives, it truly does.","late":"From his first item onward he deletes you whenever the kite stumbles, and Highlander's slow immunity plus its resets stick through all your speed. Fight only with peel around you, sleep him as he enters the fight — never after he is already on you — and accept that late duels are his, not yours.","whys":["Your Blooming Blows speed and Watch Out! poke kite him helplessly at level 1.","At 2 your mobility and burst still keep him at range and losing the trades.","Level 3 gives him Alpha Strike — untargetable mid-dash, and his own autos shorten its 20s.","At 4-5 it hinges on him dodging Watch Out! and you respecting his all-in — a skill window.","At 6, whether he eats or avoids Lilting Lullaby decides the fight — execution either way.","With his first attack-speed item he catches you the moment you stop kiting and deletes you.","Late, Highlander is 85s and makes him immune to slows — your Swirlseed stops holding him off at all."]});
